  "answer": "The vulnerability lies in the potential for a UE to become unreachable or unresponsive to network paging due to misalignment or improper handling of periodic registration update timers (T3512) and implicit de-registration timers (non-3GPP de-registration timer and non-3GPP implicit de-registration timer). Specifically, if the UE fails to initiate a periodic registration update before the T3512 timer expires, or if the non-3GPP de-registration timer expires before the AMF's non-3GPP implicit de-registration timer, the UE may be considered implicitly de-registered by the network, leading to loss of reachability and potential service disruption. This is exacerbated when the UE is in MICO mode and relies on strictly periodic registration, as the network may not enforce timely updates if the MICO mode is not properly configured or if the active time is not set. The risk is heightened in non-3GPP access where the UE may not initiate registration updates due to lack of support or configuration, resulting in a window of invisibility to the network.",
